# Coop with two players on LibreQuake's start map (L-85, DIFF-16.7): `-listen 2` gives two slots
# and `+coop 1` coop, as id's Host_FindMaxClients and stuffcmds read them; both players connect
# in frame 1 and enter in frame 4, the first at the info_player_start and the second at the
# coop start after it. They walk, turn, jump, fire and change weapon apart, one talks to the
# other, and the second goes god, so the frames run both players' physics and think functions.
# In CI (`cargo xtask sim-diff oracles/engine/routes/coop.route -- -basedir
# "$QS_TEST_ASSETS/librequake-lite"`).
engine -listen
engine 2
engine +coop
engine 1
map start
players 2
frames 72
move 0 0 0 200 0 0 0 0
move #2 0 180 0 200 0 0 0 0
frames 72
move 0 90 0 200 0 0 0 0
move #2 0 270 0 0 350 0 2 0
frames 72
move 10 180 0 200 0 0 1 2
move #2 -10 90 0 200 0 0 1 0
frames 36
cmd say hello
cmd #2 god
move 0 270 0 -200 0 0 0 1
move #2 0 45 0 200 -350 0 0 2
frames 144
